# The variant registry. Every script on `main` reads this and nothing else to decide what
# "all variants" means, so adding or retiring a variant is a one-line edit here.
#
#   <variant>  <branch>  <family>  <capabilities>
#
# `capabilities` is a comma-separated list, or `-` for none. It records workload knobs the
# branch actually implements SERVER-side, which is not the same as knobs k6 will send: k6 is
# byte-identical everywhere and sends them all, and Spring ignores unknown properties, so an
# unimplemented knob is silently discarded rather than rejected. run-suite.sh reads this to
# warn when a knob is set for variants that cannot honour it.
#
#   reserve-delay   RESERVE_DELAY_MS — `reserveDelayMs` on CreateItemRequest plus the sleep
#                   in the aggregate. Only ES-4 and TO-3 have it (verified 2026-08-06:
#                   `git grep reserveDelayMs <branch> -- src/` is empty on the other six).
#
# `variant` is the identity used everywhere downstream: it names the image tag
# (inventory-reservation-<variant>:latest, lowercased), the worktree directory, and the
# bench-results/<variant>_<scenario>_<ts>/ run directory. It must match VARIANT in that
# branch's bench.env — bench.sh builds RUN_NAME from bench.env, not from the git branch, so
# a mismatch here files results under the wrong name without any error.
#
# Order matters: run-suite.sh runs them top to bottom. Families are grouped so a single
# suite pass crosses the TO/ES boundary once rather than eight times; each crossing costs a
# full stack teardown because the two families use different compose service names.

TO-1  TO-1  TO  -
TO-2  TO-2  TO  -
TO-3  TO-3  TO  reserve-delay
TO-4  TO-4  TO  -
ES-1  ES-1  ES  -
ES-2  ES-2  ES  -
ES-3  ES-3  ES  -
ES-4  ES-4  ES  reserve-delay
